<title>INDIA: Central Indian soybean market dull, steady.</title>
<headline>Central Indian soybean market dull, steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in dull central Indian markets.</p>
<p>Arrivals of around 2,500 tonnes in the markets on Tuesday compared with levels of 20,000 tonnes per day at the same time last year, but demand appeared satisfied.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices decreased by 200 rupees per tonne on limited demand in a dull and weak local market.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $280-281 per tonne for export. Rapeseed extraction was $122-123 per tonne for ready shipment and was $115 per tonne for March-April shipment for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,250 rupees FOR Bedi Bunder and was 4,200 rupees FOR Bhavnagar. Export demand was very dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
